{"kind":{"type":"frontMatter","text":"title: \"Pull stays fast-forward only: a diverged branch goes to `git pull --rebase`\"\u000adate: 2026-09-29\u000acategory: architecture-patterns\u000amodule: rc-git-guard\u000aproblem_type: architecture_pattern\u000acomponent: infrastructure\u000aseverity: medium\u000arelated_components:\u000a  - RcGitKit\u000a  - RcGitApp\u000aapplies_when:\u000a  - \"A git operation works in a terminal, VS Code, or Zed but rc-git refuses it\"\u000a  - \"Considering an in-app rebase or merge for a diverged pull, or any guard action that rewrites commits\"\u000a  - \"Considering spawning the git binary to cover an operation gix lacks\"\u000a  - \"An action depends on user-level git config such as pull.rebase, an includeIf identity, or commit signing\"\u000a  - \"Building a command string for the user to paste or run\"\u000atags:\u000a  - gix\u000a  - pull\u000a  - rebase\u000a  - fast-forward\u000a  - diverged-branch\u000a  - isolated-open\u000a  - commit-signing\u000a  - global-config"},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":1},"runs":[{"text":"Pull stays fast-forward only: a diverged branch goes to ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"git pull --rebase","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Context","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The Sync sheet reported ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"cannot fast-forward 'master': local is 2 ahead and 4 behind; reconcile with git","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" — ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ActionError::Diverged","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). On the same checkout, ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"git pull","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in a terminal worked. Neither tool was broken; they read different config.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Terminal git read the user's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"~/.gitconfig","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which sets ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"pull.rebase = true","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", so it replayed the 2 local commits on top of the 4 upstream ones. VS Code and Zed run the git binary, so they inherit the same config: pull strategy, committer identity, and signing.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"rc-git never spawns git for a repository operation (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"clippy.toml","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"'s ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"disallowed-methods","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" bans ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"std::process::Command::new","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in the Rust crates; only the self-updater shells out, to rebuild rc-git itself), and every repository goes through an isolated open: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gix::open::Options::isolated()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"open_options","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-core/src/repo.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"open","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). Only ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".git/config","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is read; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"include","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"/","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"includeIf","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" are ignored (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"docs/safety.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", \"Untrusted repositories\"). ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"pull.rebase","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" never reaches the app.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The guard's pull only fast-forwards. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"pull_fast_forward","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions/remote/pull.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") returns ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Diverged","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" with ahead/behind counts when the local tip is not an ancestor of the upstream. Otherwise it follows the dirty-overlap order: plan the paths (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"treeapply::plan","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), refuse on any overlap (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"treeapply::verify_clean","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), write (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"treeapply::apply","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), move the ref last (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"advance_ref","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":").","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The decision was whether rc-git should do what the terminal did.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Guidance","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Keep the pull fast-forward only, and hand a divergence to git with the exact command.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Three options were weighed:","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Hand the user the command.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" Chosen.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":{"ordered":1}},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Spawn ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"git pull","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" from the app, the way the editors do.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" Rejected. It breaks the no-process rule. Git, not the guard, would write the working tree, so the dirty-overlap refusal and the ref-last ordering would no longer hold. An app launched from the Dock also has no login-shell ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"PATH","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" — the updater routes its own shell work through a login ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"zsh","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for that reason (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"mac/Sources/RcGitApp/UpdateEnvironmentLive.swift","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":").","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":{"ordered":2}},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Rebase in-process.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" Deferred as large. It needs four things the isolated open withholds or gix lacks:","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":{"ordered":3}},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Strategy.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"pull.rebase","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"pull.ff","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" live in user config, so the app cannot tell a user who wants rebase from one who wants merge.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":2,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Identity.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" Each replayed commit needs a committer. The guard takes an explicit author, else the repository's own ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"user.name","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"/","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"user.email","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"resolve_identity","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions/workfile.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). When neither is set, the app asks (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"MainWindowController.askForIdentity(completion:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", called from ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"performCommit(_:prompted:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"performStashPush(prompted:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") and saves the answer for that repository only, once the commit or stash succeeds; the repository's own config wins whenever it sets one. It cannot reproduce a per-directory identity set through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"includeIf","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":2,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Signing.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" This checkout's commits are signed (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"commit.gpgsign = true","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gpg.format = ssh","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"; recent commits show ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"G","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" under ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"git log --format=%G?","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), but the settings come from a file the user's global config pulls in with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"includeIf","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", not from ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".git/config","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", so the isolated open never sees them. The guard writes commit objects with no ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gpgsig","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" header (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"extra_headers: Vec::new()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"write_commit","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions/commit.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", and the same in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"write_stash_commits","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"stash.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). A rebase rewrites existing commits, so it would silently swap signed commits for unsigned ones, and a branch rule requiring signed commits would reject the next push. SSHSIG signing through the ssh-agent is possible — ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"russh","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is already a workspace dependency in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Cargo.toml","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and already talks to the agent for auth — but it is new work.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":2,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The replay itself.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" gix ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"=0.87.1","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" offers three-way tree merges behind its ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"merge","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" feature, which the workspace ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gix","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" entry in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Cargo.toml","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" does not enable, and has no rebase. Replaying commits, aborting on a conflict, refusing when the local side holds a merge commit or a commit already reachable from a remote-tracking ref, and recording a backup ref before the branch moves would all be written by hand.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":2,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The safety policy is already settled for it: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Action::RewriteHistory","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/lib.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") asks for a confirm and a backup ref on unpublished history, and denies published history on a protected branch (the \"rewrite unpublished/published history\" rows of the policy table in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"docs/safety.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). Revisit the rebase only if divergence happens often enough that the trip to the terminal is a real cost, and settle signing first.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"What the diverged sheet does now:","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"ReconcileCommand.rebase(workDir:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"mac/Sources/RcGitKit/SyncModel.swift","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") returns ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"cd <quoted workdir> && git pull --rebase","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". The ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"cd","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" lets the line paste into any shell and leaves that shell in the checkout when the rebase stops on a conflict. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"--rebase","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is explicit because the app cannot read ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"pull.rebase","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"; per this session's reading, current git stops and asks for a strategy when a plain ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"git pull","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" meets diverged branches with none configured. A user who prefers merge edits the line.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"ShellWord.quote","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"mac/Sources/RcGitKit/ShellWord.swift","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") leaves a word bare when every scalar is in the set Python's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"shlex.quote","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" leaves bare minus ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"=","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", and otherwise single-quotes it with each embedded quote written as ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"'\\''","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"=","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is quoted because both consumers run the word in zsh (the updater's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"/bin/zsh -lc","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", Terminal's default shell), whose EQUALS option turns ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"=ls","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" into ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"/bin/ls","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". It replaced the updater's untested ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Shell.quote","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"MainWindowController.presentDiverged(_:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" shows the guard's message and the command with Copy Command, Open in Terminal (copies, then opens ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"com.apple.Terminal","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in the checkout through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSWorkspace.open(_:withApplicationAt:configuration:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), and Close on Escape. A bare repository has no checkout to pull into and keeps the plain message. A diverged pull and a rejected push both reach this sheet: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"finish_remote","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-ffi","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" maps ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ActionError::Diverged","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ActionError::PushRejected","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" to ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"RCGIT_DIVERGED","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", matching the CLI, which exits with its diverged code for both.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The updater's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"sync()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" names the same command when the rc-git checkout diverges (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"mac/Sources/RcGitApp/UpdateEnvironmentLive.swift","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":").","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Why This Matters","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"An in-process copy of a git operation that ignores user config gives a different result from the same click in any tool that runs git, with no warning: unsigned commits where the user expects signed ones, a different committer, a rebase where they set merge. The difference surfaces later, as a rejected push or a commit under the wrong name, far from the click that caused it.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The gap already exists in a smaller form. In a repository set up for signing, commits made from the Changes tab are unsigned (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"write_commit","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"commit.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). An in-process rebase would widen that from \"new commits are unsigned\" to \"signed commits are replaced with unsigned ones\".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A handed-over command keeps both rules intact: rc-git writes only through the guard and spawns nothing, and the user's own config makes the decision, in a line they can read before running it.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"When to Apply","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Adding a guard action that writes commit objects on the user's behalf: pull with rebase or merge, amend, cherry-pick, revert, squash. Decide identity and signing first.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A feature whose correct behavior depends on a setting the isolated open never reads: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"pull.rebase","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"/","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"pull.ff","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", an ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"includeIf","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" identity, ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"commit.gpgsign","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"/","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gpg.format","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"/","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"user.signingkey","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
